Open Wayle's dashboard from an external Waybar in a real layer-shell window.

A GtkPopover is an xdg_popup tied to input received by the Wayle client. The
click belongs to Waybar, so Niri can reject or immediately dismiss that popup
even though the D-Bus request succeeds. Reparent the native dashboard content
into a monitor-local overlay layer surface for external requests instead.

Keep all other dropdowns on their existing popover path. The dashboard window
uses the configured opacity and shadow, follows the bar edge, activates its
media/network/system-stat watchers while visible, and closes before opening
Wayle settings.

